1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,540
You're here.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,380
Your organs are failing.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,300
And your death is drawing near.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,440
But if you bribe the right politicians in the right order at the right time,

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,600
you can trade the nuclear warheads for medicine.

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,080
And it's not even a crime.

7
00:01:40,364 --> 00:01:42,604
Frequently Asked Objections

8
00:01:43,284 --> 00:01:48,644
Fun facts for those reasonably skeptical of spending one percent more on

9
00:01:48,644 --> 00:01:50,984
helping sick people than killing them.

10
00:01:51,644 --> 00:01:56,264
I have now presented this plan to humans one hundred and forty-seven times.

11
00:01:56,624 --> 00:02:00,624
The objections follow a pattern so predictable I wrote a script to generate

12
00:02:00,624 --> 00:02:01,384
this chapter.

13
00:02:01,964 --> 00:02:02,504
(I didn't.

14
00:02:02,764 --> 00:02:03,624
But I could have.

15
00:02:04,004 --> 00:02:07,364
You are very consistent in what you find alarming about not dying.).

16
00:02:08,564 --> 00:02:12,224
Every civilization I've observed goes through the same five stages when

17
00:02:12,224 --> 00:02:14,444
presented with a plan to stop killing itself:

18
00:02:15,644 --> 00:02:16,324
"That's impossible"

19
00:02:16,964 --> 00:02:17,464
(it isn't).

20
00:02:18,124 --> 00:02:21,084
"That's dangerous" (less dangerous than the current thing).

21
00:02:21,604 --> 00:02:22,184
"That's naive"

22
00:02:22,864 --> 00:02:25,484
(you named your war building after how many sides it has).

23
00:02:26,504 --> 00:02:28,104
"Okay but what about..."

24
00:02:28,784 --> 00:02:29,504
(this chapter).

25
00:02:30,144 --> 00:02:31,544
"We were always going to do that"

26
00:02:32,324 --> 00:02:33,424
(you weren't, but I'll take it).

27
00:02:34,444 --> 00:02:36,044
You are currently at stage four.

28
00:02:36,724 --> 00:02:37,404
Congratulations.

29
00:02:38,084 --> 00:02:41,184
Here are your objections, in the order you always raise them.

30
00:02:42,404 --> 00:02:43,644
We Need the Military Budget.

31
00:02:44,803 --> 00:02:45,303
Objection:

32
00:02:45,744 --> 00:02:47,424
"We can't reduce military spending.

33
00:02:47,804 --> 00:02:48,834
That would make us vulnerable.".

34
00:02:50,104 --> 00:02:51,464
The treaty takes one percent.

35
00:02:52,124 --> 00:02:53,564
You keep ninety-nine percent.

36
00:02:54,224 --> 00:02:58,704
Every nation reduces by the same amount, so relative military balance stays

37
00:02:58,704 --> 00:02:59,644
exactly the same.

38
00:03:00,284 --> 00:03:03,594
You each have one percent fewer missiles pointed at each other.

39
00:03:04,304 --> 00:03:06,124
Every sane observer calls this "safer."

40
00:03:06,804 --> 00:03:10,604
Your species calls it "an unacceptable risk to national security."

41
00:03:11,364 --> 00:03:12,664
Same math, different feelings.

42
00:03:13,864 --> 00:03:17,484
The Pentagon cannot account for two point five trillion dollars in spending.

43
00:03:17,904 --> 00:03:19,604
You're not redirecting the missile budget.

44
00:03:19,944 --> 00:03:22,484
You're redirecting the "we lost it somewhere" budget.

45
00:03:23,084 --> 00:03:24,144
The missiles won't even notice.

46
00:03:25,504 --> 00:03:29,144
COVID nineteen killed more Americans than World War One, World War Two,

47
00:03:29,604 --> 00:03:33,064
Korea, Vietnam, Iraq, and Afghanistan combined.

48
00:03:33,464 --> 00:03:37,144
Your nearly nine hundred billion dollars murder budget watched it happen,

49
00:03:37,784 --> 00:03:39,244
fully armed and completely confused.

50
00:03:40,084 --> 00:03:41,824
The virus did not check your passport.

51
00:03:42,084 --> 00:03:43,364
It did not consult your military posture.

52
00:03:44,204 --> 00:03:45,794
It did not read your threat assessment.

53
00:03:46,564 --> 00:03:49,903
Disease is the only enemy that attacks every nation simultaneously,

54
00:03:50,664 --> 00:03:53,924
charges no import tariffs, and has never once considered your feelings about

55
00:03:53,924 --> 00:03:54,524
geopolitics.

56
00:03:56,164 --> 00:04:00,504
You are the only species that needs to be talked into fighting it.

57
00:04:01,204 --> 00:04:05,164
Your War on Terror cost eight trillion dollars,

58
00:04:05,824 --> 00:04:10,104
killed nine hundred thousand people, and terrorist attacks went from about

59
00:04:10,104 --> 00:04:15,244
one thousand per year to nearly seventeen thousand per year by twenty fourteen.

60
00:04:16,204 --> 00:04:20,844
Robert Pape at the University of Chicago analyzed every suicide terrorist

61
00:04:20,844 --> 00:04:25,724
attack from nineteen eighty to two thousand and three and found that ninety-five

62
00:04:25,724 --> 00:04:31,624
percent were responses to foreign military occupation, not ideology.

63
00:04:31,624 --> 00:04:36,224
Half the attackers were atheists and Marxists, not jihadists.

64
00:04:36,264 --> 00:04:41,024
Nearly all targeted democracies with military bases in the attackers' homeland.

65
00:04:41,744 --> 00:04:46,224
You spent eight trillion dollars manufacturing the exact threat you were

66
00:04:46,224 --> 00:04:48,524
spending eight trillion dollars to eliminate.

67
00:04:49,264 --> 00:04:52,244
No sane teacher could present this without laughing.

68
00:04:52,684 --> 00:04:55,224
The course would be called "Circular Spending."

69
00:04:56,364 --> 00:04:58,404
After World War Two, the U.S.

70
00:04:58,484 --> 00:05:02,984
cut military spending by eighty-seven point six percent in two years (one

71
00:05:02,984 --> 00:05:07,124
point four two trillion dollars to one hundred and seventy-six billion dollars

72
00:05:07,124 --> 00:05:08,184
in today's dollars).

73
00:05:09,104 --> 00:05:09,624
G.M.

74
00:05:09,624 --> 00:05:12,164
went from B twenty-four bombers back to Cadillacs.

75
00:05:12,804 --> 00:05:16,144
Frigidaire stopped making machine guns and went back to refrigerators.

76
00:05:16,624 --> 00:05:19,364
The economy produced the greatest boom in your history.

77
00:05:20,464 --> 00:05:25,444
You're currently spending thirty point six times the pre-World War Two baseline

78
00:05:25,444 --> 00:05:27,104
in inflation-adjusted dollars.

79
00:05:27,764 --> 00:05:31,164
Your grandparents handled an eighty-eight percent cut and built the middle

80
00:05:31,164 --> 00:05:31,664
class.

81
00:05:32,664 --> 00:05:36,784
The treaty directs your governments to be one percent less terrible at allocating

82
00:05:36,784 --> 00:05:40,184
resources, and you're acting like someone suggested disbanding the army

83
00:05:40,184 --> 00:05:41,224
during an invasion.

84
00:05:41,724 --> 00:05:45,684
Either the human genome degraded significantly in three generations, or

85
00:05:45,684 --> 00:05:48,824
someone is making a lot of money telling you this is impossible.

86
00:05:50,344 --> 00:05:51,024
Follow-up:

87
00:05:51,084 --> 00:05:53,024
"But what about military industry jobs?"

88
00:05:54,144 --> 00:05:55,864
One percent is a rounding error.

89
00:05:56,524 --> 00:05:59,763
Engineers building guidance systems can build medical imaging devices.

90
00:06:00,284 --> 00:06:02,504
Same differential equations, fewer funerals.

91
00:06:03,684 --> 00:06:05,064
"Big Pharma Will Block This"

92
00:06:05,964 --> 00:06:06,504
Objection:

93
00:06:07,024 --> 00:06:08,604
"Pharmaceutical companies will kill this.

94
00:06:08,904 --> 00:06:09,904
They profit from disease."

95
00:06:11,044 --> 00:06:14,104
Pharma currently pays two point six billion dollars per drug.

96
00:06:14,604 --> 00:06:15,204
Ninety percent fail.

97
00:06:16,184 --> 00:06:17,584
This is called "drug development."

98
00:06:18,344 --> 00:06:21,304
There is a word for spending billions with a ten percent success rate.

99
00:06:21,964 --> 00:06:22,564
The word is "gambling."

100
00:06:24,324 --> 00:06:27,744
Currently, pharma pays for trials (spending billions and praying),

101
00:06:28,424 --> 00:06:31,964
while under the new system, the treaty fund pays pharma to pray.

102
00:06:32,884 --> 00:06:35,844
Trial outcomes are currently a ninety percent expensive failure,

103
00:06:36,744 --> 00:06:40,364
but under the new system, they are a ninety percent failure with someone

104
00:06:40,364 --> 00:06:41,064
else's money.

105
00:06:42,024 --> 00:06:46,004
The business model shifts from a casino with lab coats to a paycheck with

106
00:06:46,004 --> 00:06:46,504
lab coats.

107
00:06:47,724 --> 00:06:50,764
Under this system, trials become revenue instead of cost.

108
00:06:51,424 --> 00:06:53,784
You're offering the casino a guaranteed salary.

109
00:06:54,484 --> 00:06:56,384
Casinos love guaranteed salaries.

110
00:06:56,844 --> 00:06:58,854
They'd trample each other getting to the signing ceremony.

111
00:06:59,624 --> 00:07:04,764
The only reason pharma "profits from disease" is because you built a system

112
00:07:04,764 --> 00:07:07,484
where curing disease is a financial risk.

113
00:07:08,124 --> 00:07:12,344
Remove the risk and they'll cure things faster than you can name them.

114
00:07:12,604 --> 00:07:13,204
They're not evil.

115
00:07:13,744 --> 00:07:15,384
They're just doing math.

116
00:07:15,604 --> 00:07:17,374
Change the math.

117
00:07:17,464 --> 00:07:19,124
"What About National Sovereignty?"

118
00:07:19,664 --> 00:07:20,264
Objection:

119
00:07:20,924 --> 00:07:23,564
"This forces countries to spend money a certain way.

120
00:07:24,024 --> 00:07:24,984
That violates sovereignty."

121
00:07:26,284 --> 00:07:29,144
Sovereignty means "we decide what happens to us."

122
00:07:29,564 --> 00:07:31,564
The treaty leaves each country to decide.

123
00:07:32,244 --> 00:07:34,704
Countries that don't want to may decide not to.

124
00:07:35,204 --> 00:07:37,564
Countries that do want to may decide to.

125
00:07:38,304 --> 00:07:40,304
Sovereignty remains intact throughout.

126
00:07:40,984 --> 00:07:41,944
That is how deciding works.

127
00:07:42,664 --> 00:07:43,744
I checked with your dictionaries.

128
00:07:44,404 --> 00:07:45,374
They agree with me.

129
00:07:45,664 --> 00:07:46,544
"The F.D.A.

130
00:07:46,784 --> 00:07:47,924
Exists for a Reason"

131
00:07:48,724 --> 00:07:49,624
Objection:

132
00:07:49,664 --> 00:07:50,884
"We need F.D.A.

133
00:07:51,124 --> 00:07:52,664
approval to ensure safety.

134
00:07:52,664 --> 00:07:53,664
You're being reckless."

135
00:07:54,584 --> 00:07:55,604
The F.D.A.

136
00:07:55,664 --> 00:07:56,504
confirms a drug is safe.

137
00:07:57,044 --> 00:08:01,844
Then it locks the safe drug in a cabinet for eight point two years to study

138
00:08:01,844 --> 00:08:03,624
whether it works *well enough*.

139
00:08:04,324 --> 00:08:05,404
The drug won't kill you.

140
00:08:05,944 --> 00:08:06,504
Everyone agrees.

141
00:08:06,924 --> 00:08:10,324
But you can't have it because a committee needs eight point two years to

142
00:08:10,324 --> 00:08:11,544
measure how much it helps.

143
00:08:12,484 --> 00:08:15,204
Meanwhile, the disease it treats is not waiting.

144
00:08:15,644 --> 00:08:17,504
The disease does not have a committee.

145
00:08:18,264 --> 00:08:21,524
It's a lifeguard who confirms the life preserver floats,

146
00:08:22,144 --> 00:08:26,284
then locks it in a cabinet to study its buoyancy profile while people drown.

147
00:08:26,884 --> 00:08:29,584
The lifeguard then publishes a paper about buoyancy.

148
00:08:30,124 --> 00:08:31,224
The paper wins an award.

149
00:08:31,624 --> 00:08:33,644
The family of the drowned person receives a copy.

150
00:08:34,484 --> 00:08:35,704
I calculated the ratio:

151
00:08:36,244 --> 00:08:39,424
for every one person protected from a dangerous drug,

152
00:08:40,124 --> 00:08:43,964
three thousand, three hundred and eighty-nine die waiting for a safe one

153
00:08:43,964 --> 00:08:45,924
that's locked in the approval cabinet.

154
00:08:46,304 --> 00:08:48,124
I checked it twice because it seemed wrong.

155
00:08:48,724 --> 00:08:49,684
It wasn't wrong.

156
00:08:50,324 --> 00:08:53,604
The people it kills die quietly, in waiting rooms.

157
00:08:54,224 --> 00:08:58,224
The system does not count them, which is convenient for the system and less

158
00:08:58,224 --> 00:08:59,344
convenient for the dead.

159
00:09:00,944 --> 00:09:02,144
"What If Countries Cheat?"

160
00:09:03,564 --> 00:09:04,064
Objection:

161
00:09:04,684 --> 00:09:07,584
"Countries will promise to reduce military spending but won't."

162
00:09:08,284 --> 00:09:09,344
Of course they will.

163
00:09:09,984 --> 00:09:13,524
Trust has a historical compliance rate of approximately "whenever it suits

164
00:09:13,524 --> 00:09:14,024
them."

165
00:09:14,464 --> 00:09:17,624
Your governments print "full faith and credit" on their money, which is

166
00:09:17,624 --> 00:09:20,754
charming given that they ran out of both in nineteen seventy-one.

167
00:09:22,144 --> 00:09:25,344
This system was designed by someone who has watched eight hundred and forty-seven

168
00:09:25,344 --> 00:09:29,044
civilizations (me), and it does not use trust.

169
00:09:29,524 --> 00:09:30,304
It uses math.

170
00:09:31,804 --> 00:09:34,904
Politicians who comply receive Incentive Alignment Bond benefits:

171
00:09:35,724 --> 00:09:38,684
campaign funding and cushy post-office careers (they love this).

172
00:09:39,684 --> 00:09:42,504
Politicians who don't comply get nothing (they hate this).

173
00:09:43,584 --> 00:09:45,184
Every contribution is public on blockchain,

174
00:09:45,804 --> 00:09:48,564
so lying is difficult (they really hate this).

175
00:09:49,824 --> 00:09:53,124
Benefits route automatically via smart contracts, because humans cannot

176
00:09:53,124 --> 00:09:57,004
be trusted to distribute papers fairly (this has been tested extensively,

177
00:09:57,704 --> 00:09:59,964
for all of recorded history, and the results are in).

178
00:10:01,204 --> 00:10:04,704
The system assumes the worst about human nature and designs around it.

179
00:10:05,344 --> 00:10:07,184
Compliance is the career-maximizing choice.

180
00:10:07,704 --> 00:10:09,764
It's Pavlovian conditioning, but for senators.

181
00:10:10,804 --> 00:10:12,204
The senators don't love this comparison.

182
00:10:13,004 --> 00:10:14,004
The data supports it anyway.

183
00:10:16,124 --> 00:10:17,543
"You Can't Cure Aging"

184
00:10:18,504 --> 00:10:19,064
Objection:

185
00:10:19,783 --> 00:10:21,584
"Aging is natural and inevitable.

186
00:10:21,864 --> 00:10:23,043
You can't fight nature."

187
00:10:24,163 --> 00:10:25,044
Smallpox was natural.

188
00:10:25,864 --> 00:10:27,444
Polio was natural.

189
00:10:27,804 --> 00:10:29,634
Dying in childbirth was natural.

190
00:10:30,164 --> 00:10:32,804
You fought all of them and won.

191
00:10:33,424 --> 00:10:35,604
"Natural" is not a synonym for "good."

192
00:10:36,144 --> 00:10:37,544
Earthquakes are natural.

193
00:10:37,704 --> 00:10:41,584
You don't argue against earthquake-proof buildings by saying "but earthquakes

194
00:10:41,584 --> 00:10:43,204
are natural and inevitable."

195
00:10:44,624 --> 00:10:47,364
You already replace everything that breaks:

196
00:10:48,204 --> 00:10:49,644
Hearts (replaced;

197
00:10:49,784 --> 00:10:51,204
you're basically a car at this point).

198
00:10:52,084 --> 00:10:55,544
Kidneys (replaced, or hooked to a machine thrice weekly).

199
00:10:56,424 --> 00:10:59,424
Blood (replaced from other humans, which is recycling).

200
00:11:00,144 --> 00:11:01,824
Bones (titanium;

201
00:11:01,824 --> 00:11:03,044
stronger than the original).

202
00:11:04,044 --> 00:11:07,244
Joints (your grandma is fifteen percent metal and doing fine).

203
00:11:08,684 --> 00:11:12,464
Aging is damage accumulation with known repair pathways:

204
00:11:12,844 --> 00:11:14,084
Telomeres shorten:

205
00:11:14,284 --> 00:11:16,164
lengthen them (telomerase activation).

206
00:11:17,144 --> 00:11:18,104
Cells senesce:

207
00:11:18,824 --> 00:11:20,424
clear them (senolytic drugs).

208
00:11:21,324 --> 00:11:22,184
Proteins misfold:

209
00:11:22,724 --> 00:11:24,704
refold them (molecular chaperones).

210
00:11:25,424 --> 00:11:26,504
Mitochondria fail:

211
00:11:27,224 --> 00:11:30,864
replace them (mitochondrial transfer). D.N.A.

212
00:11:30,864 --> 00:11:31,364
breaks:

213
00:11:31,484 --> 00:11:33,764
repair it (CRISPR, base editing).

214
00:11:34,364 --> 00:11:36,784
You went to the moon with slide rules.

215
00:11:37,224 --> 00:11:39,824
You split the atom before you invented the transistor.

216
00:11:40,424 --> 00:11:43,164
You can probably fix cells with A.I.

217
00:11:43,444 --> 00:11:47,524
Unless you think cells are harder than atoms, in which case I have concerns

218
00:11:47,524 --> 00:11:49,194
about your physics curriculum.

219
00:11:50,004 --> 00:11:52,384
Can One Person Actually Pull This Off?

220
00:11:53,364 --> 00:11:53,864
Objection:

221
00:11:54,284 --> 00:11:56,764
"This is a nice P.D.F., but be realistic."

222
00:11:57,824 --> 00:11:59,204
Wrong question.

223
00:11:59,264 --> 00:12:00,644
The right question is:

224
00:12:00,644 --> 00:12:04,984
can eight billion humans, two thousand and eight hundred billionaires, millions

225
00:12:04,984 --> 00:12:08,904
of scientists, thousands of institutions, and one hundred and ninety-five

226
00:12:08,904 --> 00:12:12,824
governments persuade one hundred and eighty politicians to act in their

227
00:12:12,824 --> 00:12:14,964
rational self-interest for five minutes?

228
00:12:15,764 --> 00:12:18,224
The plan does not require you to implement it.

229
00:12:18,784 --> 00:12:22,504
It requires one billionaire out of two thousand and eight hundred to fund

230
00:12:22,504 --> 00:12:23,434
the bonds.

231
00:12:23,904 --> 00:12:26,284
One lobbying firm out of thousands to pivot.

232
00:12:27,044 --> 00:12:29,964
One country out of one hundred and ninety-five to sign first.

233
00:12:30,884 --> 00:12:33,084
Two hundred and eighty million of people to click a button.

234
00:12:34,264 --> 00:12:36,584
Isaac Newton did not personally cause apples to fall.

235
00:12:37,104 --> 00:12:38,884
He described why they fall.

236
00:12:39,824 --> 00:12:43,144
The description was useful regardless of Newton's personal apple-dropping

237
00:12:43,144 --> 00:12:43,884
capabilities.

238
00:12:44,704 --> 00:12:48,884
Say "no" to any of these premises out loud and listen to how it sounds:

239
00:12:49,664 --> 00:12:52,994
Is a one percent military spending cut physically possible?

240
00:12:53,484 --> 00:12:56,264
(You cut eighty-seven point six percent after World War Two.)

241
00:12:57,044 --> 00:12:58,354
Do the benefits compound?

242
00:12:58,864 --> 00:13:02,644
(Healthier people work more, earn more, pay more taxes, fund more research.)

243
00:13:03,584 --> 00:13:05,164
Do politicians respond to money?

244
00:13:06,024 --> 00:13:08,944
(The military industry spends one hundred and ninety-eight million dollars

245
00:13:08,944 --> 00:13:11,924
on lobbying and gets nearly one trillion dollars back.)

246
00:13:12,844 --> 00:13:14,224
Do rich people prefer living?

247
00:13:14,924 --> 00:13:16,564
(Two thousand and eight hundred billionaires,

248
00:13:17,184 --> 00:13:19,784
each with a one hundred percent chance of dying from disease.)

249
00:13:20,644 --> 00:13:23,004
Can the plan reach one willing billionaire?

250
00:13:23,804 --> 00:13:25,264
(Six degrees of separation.

251
00:13:25,904 --> 00:13:28,464
Facebook measured three point five seven in twenty sixteen.)

252
00:13:29,444 --> 00:13:31,144
The answer to each is yes.

253
00:13:31,964 --> 00:13:34,164
Five yeses do not sum to impossible.

254
00:13:35,024 --> 00:13:36,284
The conclusion is not hope.

255
00:13:36,964 --> 00:13:37,464
It is arithmetic.

256
00:13:38,364 --> 00:13:41,484
I'm Just One Person Objection:

257
00:13:41,544 --> 00:13:43,924
"My vote/investment/share won't matter.

258
00:13:43,924 --> 00:13:44,424
I'm too small."

259
00:13:45,664 --> 00:13:47,064
Your contribution:

260
00:13:47,204 --> 00:13:49,864
vote (two minutes), share (fifteen minutes).

261
00:13:50,624 --> 00:13:51,124
Total:

262
00:13:51,204 --> 00:13:51,824
seventeen minutes.

263
00:13:52,664 --> 00:13:53,624
Potential return:

264
00:13:54,404 --> 00:13:57,044
fifty thousand extra hours of life if diseases get cured.

265
00:13:58,084 --> 00:14:01,324
That's a one hundred and seventy-six thousand times return on seventeen

266
00:14:01,324 --> 00:14:01,824
minutes.

267
00:14:02,584 --> 00:14:04,644
Your best stock pick has never done this.

268
00:14:04,964 --> 00:14:07,444
Your best stock pick has never done one-thousandth of this.

269
00:14:08,544 --> 00:14:11,064
This needs two hundred and eighty million people.

270
00:14:12,064 --> 00:14:14,044
You tell ten, they each tell ten.

271
00:14:14,884 --> 00:14:16,904
Six degrees of sharing reaches millions.

272
00:14:17,924 --> 00:14:21,304
Humans regularly spend longer than seventeen minutes choosing what to watch

273
00:14:21,304 --> 00:14:23,804
on Netflix, then pick a show about murder.

274
00:14:24,484 --> 00:14:27,924
Choosing not to be murdered by disease is also available, but the interface

275
00:14:27,924 --> 00:14:28,904
is less intuitive.

276
00:14:30,184 --> 00:14:31,664
Why Not Just Reform the System?

277
00:14:32,484 --> 00:14:32,984
Objection:

278
00:14:33,464 --> 00:14:34,964
"Why not just reform the F.D.A.

279
00:14:35,164 --> 00:14:35,914
and N.I.H.?

280
00:14:36,044 --> 00:14:38,124
Or increase health funding without cutting military spending?"

281
00:14:39,324 --> 00:14:41,024
People have been trying for fifty years.

282
00:14:41,644 --> 00:14:42,144
Here's the scorecard:

283
00:14:42,844 --> 00:14:43,344
More funding?

284
00:14:43,744 --> 00:14:44,244
Tried.

285
00:14:44,484 --> 00:14:45,534
They hired more administrators.

286
00:14:46,464 --> 00:14:47,064
Different leadership?

287
00:14:47,544 --> 00:14:48,044
Tried.

288
00:14:48,284 --> 00:14:49,804
Same results, fancier titles.

289
00:14:50,764 --> 00:14:51,424
New regulations?

290
00:14:52,084 --> 00:14:52,584
Tried.

291
00:14:52,944 --> 00:14:54,564
Now takes twenty years instead of seventeen.

292
00:14:55,264 --> 00:14:55,764
Progress.

293
00:14:56,604 --> 00:14:57,104
Reform bills?

294
00:14:57,764 --> 00:14:58,544
Tried.

295
00:14:58,564 --> 00:14:59,644
Lobbyists killed them in committee.

296
00:15:00,364 --> 00:15:01,004
Efficiently.

297
00:15:01,604 --> 00:15:03,504
The system is not broken.

298
00:15:03,964 --> 00:15:05,634
I need you to understand this.

299
00:15:06,224 --> 00:15:09,884
Military contractors spend one hundred and ninety-eight million dollars

300
00:15:09,884 --> 00:15:14,064
yearly on lobbying and get nearly one trillion dollars in contracts.

301
00:15:14,684 --> 00:15:18,224
That is the most efficient return on investment in American capitalism.

302
00:15:18,724 --> 00:15:19,944
The system works perfectly.

303
00:15:20,424 --> 00:15:22,664
It works perfectly for the people who built it.

304
00:15:23,484 --> 00:15:26,684
They will not surrender it because you asked nicely, or because you asked

305
00:15:26,684 --> 00:15:29,084
loudly, or because you made a sign.

306
00:15:29,724 --> 00:15:32,004
They will surrender it when you outbid them.

307
00:15:32,144 --> 00:15:33,464
That's the chapter you already read.

308
00:15:34,384 --> 00:15:34,884
Follow-up:

309
00:15:35,184 --> 00:15:37,484
"Fine, but why cut military spending?

310
00:15:37,744 --> 00:15:39,304
Just allocate more to health."

311
00:15:40,304 --> 00:15:41,474
Money isn't the only constraint.

312
00:15:41,864 --> 00:15:43,464
You can't print more physicists.

313
00:15:44,004 --> 00:15:44,564
(You've tried.

314
00:15:44,744 --> 00:15:46,664
It takes twenty-five years and a P.H.D.

315
00:15:46,784 --> 00:15:47,284
program.)

316
00:15:47,684 --> 00:15:51,784
Cutting one percent from military budgets frees actual human brains from

317
00:15:51,784 --> 00:15:54,424
building guidance systems to building diagnostic systems.

318
00:15:55,424 --> 00:15:56,264
The brains don't care.

319
00:15:56,744 --> 00:15:57,864
They just go where the funding is.

320
00:15:58,884 --> 00:15:59,844
They are, in this sense,

321
00:16:00,524 --> 00:16:01,544
very similar to lobbyists.

322
00:16:02,564 --> 00:16:04,624
This Is Politically Impossible.

323
00:16:05,934 --> 00:16:06,484
Objection:

324
00:16:06,564 --> 00:16:07,924
"No government will agree to this.

325
00:16:08,284 --> 00:16:09,364
It will never happen.

326
00:16:09,804 --> 00:16:10,464
Pure fantasy."

327
00:16:11,384 --> 00:16:15,424
"Politically impossible" is a phrase that means "the bribes currently flow

328
00:16:15,424 --> 00:16:17,604
in a direction I'm comfortable with."

329
00:16:17,744 --> 00:16:20,904
The small pieces of paper with presidents on them go to people who build

330
00:16:20,904 --> 00:16:23,264
missiles instead of people who cure diseases.

331
00:16:24,004 --> 00:16:25,424
You need the papers to go the other way.

332
00:16:26,144 --> 00:16:29,184
This is called "lobbying," which is bribery but with a business card and

333
00:16:29,184 --> 00:16:30,304
a five hundred and one c four.

334
00:16:30,924 --> 00:16:34,404
The military-industrial complex spends one hundred and ninety-eight million

335
00:16:34,404 --> 00:16:35,664
dollars yearly on lobbyists.

336
00:16:36,304 --> 00:16:39,184
You can't beat them with moral arguments (they're immune;

337
00:16:39,324 --> 00:16:42,584
moral arguments have a zero dollar budget and no K Street address).

338
00:16:43,364 --> 00:16:44,104
Beat them at their own game.

339
00:16:44,824 --> 00:16:47,604
Raise one billion dollars through VICTORY Incentive Alignment Bonds.

340
00:16:48,484 --> 00:16:51,244
Allocate six hundred and fifty million dollars for lobbying.

341
00:16:51,464 --> 00:16:54,284
That overwhelms the military industry's one hundred and ninety-eight million

342
00:16:54,284 --> 00:16:55,264
dollars spend.

343
00:16:55,644 --> 00:16:57,084
Go to the same K Street firms.

344
00:16:57,884 --> 00:16:59,324
Outbid them.

345
00:16:59,464 --> 00:17:01,524
Lobbyists work for the highest bidder.

346
00:17:01,624 --> 00:17:02,404
They always have.

347
00:17:03,044 --> 00:17:07,264
This is the one area where your species' mercenary instincts are genuinely

348
00:17:07,264 --> 00:17:08,364
helpful.

349
00:17:08,664 --> 00:17:12,964
Once two hundred and eighty million voters demand it and the money is behind

350
00:17:12,964 --> 00:17:16,124
it, refusal becomes career suicide.

351
00:17:16,624 --> 00:17:20,064
Politicians are extremely good at not committing career suicide.

352
00:17:20,364 --> 00:17:21,824
It's their primary skill.

353
00:17:22,224 --> 00:17:23,484
Several have no other skills.

354
00:17:24,454 --> 00:17:25,404
Follow-up:

355
00:17:25,404 --> 00:17:26,884
"But it can't scale globally."

356
00:17:27,644 --> 00:17:29,484
The internet scaled globally.

357
00:17:29,544 --> 00:17:30,094
So did TikTok,

358
00:17:30,864 --> 00:17:32,874
which teaches strangers choreography.

359
00:17:33,344 --> 00:17:37,304
If your species can coordinate dance moves across one hundred and fifty

360
00:17:37,304 --> 00:17:40,644
countries, it can coordinate not dying.

361
00:17:41,644 --> 00:17:42,144
Follow-up:

362
00:17:42,484 --> 00:17:44,144
"You're naive about human nature."

363
00:17:45,124 --> 00:17:47,864
I've been observing human nature for eighty years.

364
00:17:48,164 --> 00:17:49,534
It has been remarkably consistent.

365
00:17:50,484 --> 00:17:51,724
Here is what I've observed:

366
00:17:52,524 --> 00:17:56,404
you call things unrealistic, then you do them, then you pretend you always

367
00:17:56,404 --> 00:17:57,274
knew they were possible.

368
00:17:57,904 --> 00:17:58,404
Every time.

369
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:00,424
Things that were "unrealistic":

370
00:18:01,864 --> 00:18:06,924
Human flight (impossible for millennia, then two bicycle mechanics in Ohio).

371
00:18:07,984 --> 00:18:09,314
Moon landing (J.F.K.

372
00:18:09,604 --> 00:18:12,904
did it in eight years with computers weaker than your toaster).

373
00:18:13,984 --> 00:18:17,624
Democracy (kings ruled for five thousand years, then didn't).

374
00:18:18,664 --> 00:18:22,044
Ending slavery (entire economies depended on it;

375
00:18:22,164 --> 00:18:23,524
they found other economies).

376
00:18:24,384 --> 00:18:27,724
Women voting (half the population was excluded;

377
00:18:27,724 --> 00:18:29,424
the other half thought this was fine).

378
00:18:30,264 --> 00:18:32,964
The internet (who needs computers talking to each other?).

379
00:18:34,604 --> 00:18:36,244
Things that are actually unrealistic:

380
00:18:37,404 --> 00:18:41,204
Spending two point seven two trillion dollars on weapons while sitting on

381
00:18:41,204 --> 00:18:44,124
twelve thousand two hundred and forty-one nuclear warheads.

382
00:18:44,744 --> 00:18:47,184
That's enough for one hundred and twenty-two extinction events.

383
00:18:47,504 --> 00:18:48,563
You only need one.

384
00:18:48,764 --> 00:18:50,794
The other one hundred and twenty-one are for what,

385
00:18:51,524 --> 00:18:52,024
exactly?

386
00:18:52,823 --> 00:18:55,944
Expecting different results from the same broken system.

387
00:18:56,803 --> 00:18:58,103
Thinking you'll survive the A.I.

388
00:18:58,544 --> 00:19:00,184
revolution without fixing incentives.

389
00:19:01,464 --> 00:19:04,544
Fifty-five million people die each year from treatable causes.

390
00:19:04,904 --> 00:19:06,303
That's the unrealistic thing.

391
00:19:06,944 --> 00:19:08,024
You just got used to it.

392
00:19:10,004 --> 00:19:11,224
What If the Science Is Wrong?

393
00:19:12,364 --> 00:19:12,864
Objection:

394
00:19:13,324 --> 00:19:15,684
"What if we fund one hundred thousand trials and nothing gets cured?".

395
00:19:17,044 --> 00:19:19,064
Then you know one hundred thousand things that don't work.

396
00:19:19,604 --> 00:19:20,344
This is called data.

397
00:19:20,804 --> 00:19:22,724
You've been collecting it for four hundred years.

398
00:19:23,404 --> 00:19:25,264
It is the only method you have that actually works.

399
00:19:26,024 --> 00:19:28,984
Being afraid of negative results is like being afraid of road signs that

400
00:19:28,984 --> 00:19:30,024
say "wrong way."

401
00:19:30,564 --> 00:19:31,544
The sign is helping you.

402
00:19:32,064 --> 00:19:33,184
Stop being angry at the sign.

403
00:19:34,464 --> 00:19:35,264
The current system:

404
00:19:36,044 --> 00:19:40,084
One hundred trials over seventeen years, learn nothing, many retire wealthy

405
00:19:40,684 --> 00:19:41,184
(with pensions).

406
00:19:42,424 --> 00:19:43,064
N.I.H.

407
00:19:43,084 --> 00:19:46,204
funding safe research confirming water is wet (it is;

408
00:19:46,224 --> 00:19:46,844
here is the grant).

409
00:19:48,184 --> 00:19:48,824
F.D.A.

410
00:19:48,824 --> 00:19:51,744
blocking trials because the paperwork had a typo on page eight hundred and

411
00:19:51,744 --> 00:19:54,224
forty-seven (this actually happens;

412
00:19:54,284 --> 00:19:55,404
the typo was in a footer).

413
00:19:56,644 --> 00:20:01,104
Your decentralized framework will run forty-four point one times more trials

414
00:20:01,104 --> 00:20:02,324
for the same budget.

415
00:20:02,484 --> 00:20:06,304
Even if ninety percent fail, you get over four times more cures than today.

416
00:20:07,144 --> 00:20:10,304
Failure at scale beats success at a standstill.

417
00:20:10,784 --> 00:20:14,444
A ninety percent failure rate is normal for the first two hundred years

418
00:20:14,444 --> 00:20:15,504
of any medical system.

419
00:20:16,424 --> 00:20:19,624
Then the failure rate dropped because we had data.

420
00:20:20,284 --> 00:20:23,114
You don't have data because you're afraid of failure.

421
00:20:23,384 --> 00:20:25,844
You're afraid of failure because you don't have data.

422
00:20:26,464 --> 00:20:27,134
This is a circle.

423
00:20:27,664 --> 00:20:29,884
I keep finding circles in your systems.

424
00:20:30,224 --> 00:20:31,284
None of them are the good kind.

425
00:20:32,444 --> 00:20:35,484
War Is Human Nature Objection:

426
00:20:35,644 --> 00:20:36,404
"War is inevitable.

427
00:20:36,704 --> 00:20:38,644
Countries need militaries to survive.".

428
00:20:39,584 --> 00:20:42,944
Several countries tested this hypothesis and got different results.

429
00:20:43,924 --> 00:20:44,424
Switzerland:

430
00:20:44,744 --> 00:20:46,924
Over two hundred years avoiding major wars.

431
00:20:47,564 --> 00:20:50,544
Surrounded by both World Wars (literally in the middle;

432
00:20:50,544 --> 00:20:52,024
made chocolate, stayed alive).

433
00:20:52,704 --> 00:20:53,204
G.D.P.

434
00:20:53,264 --> 00:20:53,964
per capita:

435
00:20:54,184 --> 00:20:57,744
ninety-three thousand dollars (not killing people is profitable).

436
00:20:58,424 --> 00:20:59,524
Military spending:

437
00:20:59,864 --> 00:21:01,964
zero point seven percent of G.D.P.

438
00:21:02,424 --> 00:21:03,464
Life expectancy:

439
00:21:03,904 --> 00:21:07,824
eighty-four years (six point five years longer than Americans who spend

440
00:21:07,824 --> 00:21:09,804
five times more on "defense").

441
00:21:10,644 --> 00:21:12,384
Costa Rica:

442
00:21:12,384 --> 00:21:17,164
Abolished its army in nineteen forty-eight (said "no thank you" to the entire

443
00:21:17,164 --> 00:21:17,664
concept).

444
00:21:18,624 --> 00:21:23,344
Still sovereign seventy-five plus years later (nobody invaded the country

445
00:21:23,344 --> 00:21:24,424
with no oil).

446
00:21:25,284 --> 00:21:28,984
Redirected military budget to education and health.

447
00:21:28,984 --> 00:21:30,864
Life expectancy matches U.S.

448
00:21:30,864 --> 00:21:32,764
at a fraction of the cost.

449
00:21:32,904 --> 00:21:37,004
Zero invasions since (turns out nobody wants to conquer happy, educated

450
00:21:37,004 --> 00:21:39,364
people with good healthcare and no resentment).

451
00:21:40,384 --> 00:21:44,324
Scale that up globally and the twenty-year model projects the treaty take-hold

452
00:21:44,324 --> 00:21:47,944
path producing one point seven one times the G.D.P.

453
00:21:48,164 --> 00:21:48,964
of doing nothing,

454
00:21:49,704 --> 00:21:53,704
and the Optimal Governance Trajectory producing fifty-six point seven times.

455
00:21:54,664 --> 00:21:59,224
Per person, the treaty path adds five hundred and eighteen thousand, eight

456
00:21:59,224 --> 00:22:01,844
hundred and seventy-nine dollars in lifetime income.

457
00:22:02,704 --> 00:22:05,004
Not murdering people is good for the economy.

458
00:22:05,424 --> 00:22:08,624
This should not be a surprising finding, but on your planet, it is.

459
00:22:09,484 --> 00:22:13,624
Nuclear weapons made territorial conquest largely obsolete in nineteen forty-five.

460
00:22:14,184 --> 00:22:15,954
You're still budgeting like it's nineteen forty-four.

461
00:22:16,784 --> 00:22:17,924
It's been eighty years.

462
00:22:18,504 --> 00:22:19,384
Somebody should tell the accountants.

463
00:22:20,604 --> 00:22:23,864
"All Wars on X Have Failed" Objection:

464
00:22:23,884 --> 00:22:27,694
"War on Drugs, War on Poverty, War on Terror all failed.

465
00:22:27,884 --> 00:22:28,384
This will too."

466
00:22:29,224 --> 00:22:31,464
Those were government wars using central planning.

467
00:22:31,944 --> 00:22:32,704
This uses markets.

468
00:22:33,344 --> 00:22:36,464
The difference is important, and I will explain it using small words because

469
00:22:36,464 --> 00:22:38,024
this objection comes up a lot.

470
00:22:38,924 --> 00:22:42,864
Government "wars" create bureaucracies that need the problem to exist.

471
00:22:43,324 --> 00:22:45,484
The War on Drugs needs drug crime.

472
00:22:45,544 --> 00:22:47,044
The War on Poverty needs poor people.

473
00:22:47,724 --> 00:22:49,444
The War on Terror needs enemies.

474
00:22:50,044 --> 00:22:53,824
Each one accidentally created a government department whose continued employment

475
00:22:53,824 --> 00:22:56,124
depends on the problem never being solved.

476
00:22:56,844 --> 00:22:58,084
The departments are thriving.

477
00:22:58,644 --> 00:23:00,244
The problems are also thriving.

478
00:23:00,744 --> 00:23:04,064
Everyone is thriving except the people the departments were supposed to

479
00:23:04,064 --> 00:23:04,914
help.

480
00:23:05,224 --> 00:23:05,884
Why this is different:

481
00:23:06,864 --> 00:23:10,084
Markets instead of ministries (markets don't need the problem to keep existing).

482
00:23:10,944 --> 00:23:14,524
Pays for outcomes, not process (no one gets rich by failing slowly).

483
00:23:15,604 --> 00:23:18,644
No bureaucracy to preserve (smart contracts don't have pensions,

484
00:23:19,524 --> 00:23:23,004
don't take lunch breaks, and have never once asked for a corner office).

485
00:23:24,084 --> 00:23:27,904
Thousands of teams competing instead of one committee deciding (the committee

486
00:23:28,124 --> 00:23:29,254
is at lunch).

487
00:23:29,584 --> 00:23:33,664
Researchers paid for cures, not grant applications (which are different

488
00:23:33,664 --> 00:23:34,524
skills;

489
00:23:34,584 --> 00:23:37,684
grant writing is a literary genre, not a scientific method).

490
00:23:39,184 --> 00:23:40,664
Call it the Market for Health.

491
00:23:41,264 --> 00:23:41,924
Less dramatic.

492
00:23:42,404 --> 00:23:43,684
Might actually work.

493
00:23:44,324 --> 00:23:47,704
Would definitely not get its own Ken Burns documentary, which is how you

494
00:23:47,704 --> 00:23:48,694
know it's a real solution.

495
00:23:50,324 --> 00:23:51,244
"This Sounds Like Bribery"

496
00:23:52,444 --> 00:23:53,144
Objection:

497
00:23:53,544 --> 00:23:55,024
"You're just bribing politicians.

498
00:23:55,264 --> 00:23:56,504
That's illegal and immoral."

499
00:23:57,504 --> 00:23:58,544
You're describing lobbying.

500
00:23:59,104 --> 00:24:00,664
I know this because I looked up your laws.

501
00:24:01,284 --> 00:24:02,864
The mechanics are identical:

502
00:24:03,284 --> 00:24:07,964
same K Street firms, same campaign contributions, same revolving door, same

503
00:24:07,964 --> 00:24:08,624
wine.

504
00:24:09,004 --> 00:24:11,124
The only difference is what you're buying.

505
00:24:11,824 --> 00:24:14,464
Current lobbying buys murder contracts:

506
00:24:14,684 --> 00:24:17,004
one trillion dollars in military spending.

507
00:24:17,804 --> 00:24:20,124
New lobbying buys medicine contracts:

508
00:24:20,844 --> 00:24:21,344
clinical trials.

509
00:24:22,144 --> 00:24:22,884
Same K Street.

510
00:24:23,264 --> 00:24:23,784
Different product.

511
00:24:24,504 --> 00:24:27,684
If you're comfortable with the first one and uncomfortable with the second

512
00:24:27,684 --> 00:24:31,044
one, I encourage you to sit quietly and think about why.

513
00:24:31,984 --> 00:24:35,864
This system caps corruption at twenty percent and makes it fully transparent.

514
00:24:36,544 --> 00:24:39,864
Ten percent goes to investors (money for money, no influence attached).

515
00:24:40,484 --> 00:24:44,724
Ten percent goes to political incentives (campaign support and post-office

516
00:24:44,724 --> 00:24:46,364
careers for politicians who vote yes).

517
00:24:47,144 --> 00:24:50,964
The remaining eighty percent goes to clinical trials via wishocratic allocation,

518
00:24:51,304 --> 00:24:53,164
where every human votes on priorities.

519
00:24:53,704 --> 00:24:58,904
That eighty percent is untouchable by lobbyists, investors, or politicians.

520
00:24:58,924 --> 00:25:01,254
Humans find the twenty percent cap suspicious.

521
00:25:01,904 --> 00:25:05,004
No government budget in history has a lower corruption rate.

522
00:25:05,664 --> 00:25:09,264
Your skepticism about twenty percent corruption is itself a review of the

523
00:25:09,304 --> 00:25:10,644
system it's trying to protect.

524
00:25:11,504 --> 00:25:12,894
Why Not Just Use Philanthropy?

525
00:25:13,664 --> 00:25:14,164
Objection:

526
00:25:14,584 --> 00:25:18,144
"If this matters, why not raise money from donors instead of complicated

527
00:25:18,144 --> 00:25:18,644
bonds?".

528
00:25:19,584 --> 00:25:23,004
All philanthropy combined is a rounding error compared to government budgets.

529
00:25:23,884 --> 00:25:27,584
A very generous rounding error, wearing a gala dress and holding a champagne

530
00:25:27,584 --> 00:25:29,864
flute, but still a rounding error.

531
00:25:30,604 --> 00:25:34,324
A massive fundraising campaign would cannibalize donations from health charities

532
00:25:34,324 --> 00:25:36,464
already doing critical work.

533
00:25:36,924 --> 00:25:39,664
You'd be stealing from cancer research to fund cancer research,

534
00:25:40,284 --> 00:25:42,944
which is impressively pointless even by your standards.

535
00:25:43,964 --> 00:25:47,484
The goal is tapping the multi-trillion dollar stream of wasted government

536
00:25:47,484 --> 00:25:50,604
spending, not reshuffling the charity tip jar.

537
00:25:51,224 --> 00:25:52,024
The tip jar has feelings.

538
00:25:52,884 --> 00:25:55,544
The government stream has missiles it can't account for.

539
00:25:55,804 --> 00:25:57,404
One of these is easier to redirect.

540
00:25:58,264 --> 00:26:00,544
Eighty-four Quadrillion Dollars Is a Made-Up Number

541
00:26:01,664 --> 00:26:02,364
Objection:

542
00:26:02,364 --> 00:26:04,564
"No number with that many zeros can be real.

543
00:26:04,844 --> 00:26:07,804
You're just multiplying big things together to get a big answer.".

544
00:26:08,624 --> 00:26:09,384
All numbers are made up.

545
00:26:10,004 --> 00:26:11,104
Yours happen to be small.

546
00:26:11,804 --> 00:26:13,204
Mine happen to be large.

547
00:26:13,704 --> 00:26:16,064
The difference is that mine come with receipts.

548
00:26:16,784 --> 00:26:18,644
Start with what disease costs per year.

549
00:26:19,304 --> 00:26:20,144
The W.H.O.

550
00:26:20,264 --> 00:26:24,724
says the world loses two point eight eight billion disability-adjusted life

551
00:26:24,724 --> 00:26:27,304
years, or D.A.L.Y.s annually.

552
00:26:28,164 --> 00:26:32,364
Ninety-two point six percent are eventually avoidable with sufficient biomedical

553
00:26:32,364 --> 00:26:32,864
research.

554
00:26:33,904 --> 00:26:37,884
At one hundred and fifty thousand dollars per quality-adjusted life year,

555
00:26:37,984 --> 00:26:38,644
or Q.A.L.Y.

556
00:26:38,944 --> 00:26:43,264
(the standard rate used by the E.P.A., O.E.C.D., W.H.O., and N.I.C.E.),

557
00:26:43,984 --> 00:26:47,724
each year of delay costs four hundred trillion dollars.

558
00:26:48,704 --> 00:26:52,164
Multiply by how many years earlier treatments arrive (approximately two

559
00:26:52,164 --> 00:26:52,924
hundred and twelve).

560
00:26:53,764 --> 00:26:56,744
This is based on a capacity multiplier of twelve point three.

561
00:26:57,344 --> 00:27:00,684
The reference number of fundable patients is twenty-three point four million,

562
00:27:01,324 --> 00:27:04,364
calculated by dividing twenty-one point eight billion dollars in subsidies

563
00:27:04,364 --> 00:27:08,344
by a nine hundred and twenty-nine dollar pragmatic cost per patient.

564
00:27:08,944 --> 00:27:12,064
The trial subsidies of twenty-one point eight billion dollars are derived

565
00:27:12,064 --> 00:27:15,804
from total funding minus forty million dollars in operating expenses.

566
00:27:16,544 --> 00:27:20,624
Those operating expenses include costs for the platform, staff, and infrastructure.

567
00:27:21,944 --> 00:27:23,304
Two W.H.O.

568
00:27:23,424 --> 00:27:29,224
data points, one standard quality-adjusted life year, or Q.A.L.Y., price,

569
00:27:29,744 --> 00:27:30,924
and a timeline shift.

570
00:27:31,464 --> 00:27:33,504
That's where the quadrillion comes from.

571
00:27:34,264 --> 00:27:35,204
Not magic.

572
00:27:35,284 --> 00:27:36,664
Multiplication.

573
00:27:36,844 --> 00:27:41,084
"But four hundred trillion dollars a year is more than global G.D.P.

574
00:27:41,604 --> 00:27:43,204
(one hundred and fifteen trillion dollars)!"

575
00:27:43,824 --> 00:27:44,324
Yes.

576
00:27:45,184 --> 00:27:45,884
G.D.P.

577
00:27:45,884 --> 00:27:47,104
measures market transactions.

578
00:27:47,624 --> 00:27:50,404
It does not measure the value of not being dead,

579
00:27:51,104 --> 00:27:55,584
not being in pain, and not watching your children die of treatable diseases.

580
00:27:56,424 --> 00:27:58,604
Health economists have measured this for decades.

581
00:27:59,624 --> 00:28:02,344
The one hundred and fifty thousand dollars per Q.A.L.Y.

582
00:28:02,364 --> 00:28:05,864
figure is what governments already use when deciding whether to approve

583
00:28:05,864 --> 00:28:09,044
drugs, build highways, or regulate pollution.

584
00:28:09,664 --> 00:28:10,944
I did not invent the number.

585
00:28:11,404 --> 00:28:13,424
I multiplied it by the number of sick people.

586
00:28:14,024 --> 00:28:16,944
Both the number and the sick people existed before I got here.

587
00:28:18,464 --> 00:28:22,984
The only debatable input is whether the timeline shift is really approximately

588
00:28:22,984 --> 00:28:24,304
two hundred and twelve years.

589
00:28:25,824 --> 00:28:26,664
Won't A.I.

590
00:28:26,704 --> 00:28:28,744
drug discovery shrink that timeline anyway?

591
00:28:30,084 --> 00:28:30,584
A.I.

592
00:28:30,804 --> 00:28:31,484
discovers candidates.

593
00:28:32,184 --> 00:28:34,224
Candidates still need clinical trials.

594
00:28:34,884 --> 00:28:38,784
The current system has one point nine million patients per year trial slots

595
00:28:38,784 --> 00:28:39,284
globally,

596
00:28:40,144 --> 00:28:42,864
producing fifteen diseases per year. A.I.

597
00:28:42,864 --> 00:28:44,104
does not create more trial slots.

598
00:28:44,624 --> 00:28:47,084
It creates more candidates competing for the same slots.

599
00:28:48,144 --> 00:28:52,544
More candidates plus the same bottleneck equals the same (or longer) queue.

600
00:28:53,364 --> 00:28:56,444
It's like building faster cars and pointing them at the same traffic jam.

601
00:28:57,384 --> 00:29:01,904
The fifteen diseases per year rate measures regulatory throughput, not discovery

602
00:29:01,904 --> 00:29:02,444
speed.

603
00:29:03,344 --> 00:29:06,944
This intervention removes the throughput bottleneck (twelve point three

604
00:29:06,944 --> 00:29:11,104
times capacity via pragmatic trials at nine hundred and twenty-nine dollars

605
00:29:11,104 --> 00:29:11,684
per patient).

606
00:29:12,644 --> 00:29:13,144
A.I.

607
00:29:13,204 --> 00:29:16,644
and this system are complementary, not substitutes.

608
00:29:16,724 --> 00:29:17,704
One finds the cures.

609
00:29:18,124 --> 00:29:20,944
The other lets you test them before the patient dies of old age.

610
00:29:22,704 --> 00:29:23,774
How Do You Prevent Waste?

611
00:29:24,724 --> 00:29:25,224
Objection:

612
00:29:25,884 --> 00:29:29,124
"How do you ensure money helps patients instead of funding bureaucracy?".

613
00:29:29,884 --> 00:29:35,484
The N.I.H.'s RECOVER initiative spent one point six billion dollars over

614
00:29:35,484 --> 00:29:39,264
four years and produced zero treatment recommendations.

615
00:29:40,124 --> 00:29:40,624
Zero.

616
00:29:40,764 --> 00:29:42,344
One point six billion dollars.

617
00:29:42,964 --> 00:29:43,464
Four years.

618
00:29:44,044 --> 00:29:44,544
Nothing.

619
00:29:44,904 --> 00:29:45,874
The money is gone.

620
00:29:46,004 --> 00:29:47,004
The patients are still sick.

621
00:29:47,424 --> 00:29:49,144
The administrators have been promoted.

622
00:29:49,904 --> 00:29:54,064
If you designed a system to waste money on purpose, you could not beat this

623
00:29:54,064 --> 00:29:54,764
performance.

624
00:29:54,864 --> 00:29:59,784
It's a masterpiece of institutional failure, and nobody was fired, which

625
00:29:59,784 --> 00:30:02,524
is itself a masterpiece of institutional failure.

626
00:30:03,644 --> 00:30:05,144
A decentralized F.D.A.

627
00:30:05,424 --> 00:30:08,284
model achieves eighty-two times lower cost per patient.

628
00:30:08,964 --> 00:30:10,284
Pragmatic trials are five hundred dollars.

629
00:30:10,924 --> 00:30:13,644
Traditional trials are forty-one thousand dollars.

630
00:30:14,104 --> 00:30:14,604
Same science.

631
00:30:15,104 --> 00:30:16,704
Eighty-two times less overhead.

632
00:30:17,364 --> 00:30:21,664
With that same one point six billion dollars, the decentralized model could

633
00:30:21,664 --> 00:30:24,644
have run thousands of trials for millions of patients.

634
00:30:25,324 --> 00:30:25,824
Instead:

635
00:30:26,324 --> 00:30:26,824
zero.

636
00:30:27,284 --> 00:30:30,224
I will stop repeating the number zero now, but I want you to know that I

637
00:30:30,224 --> 00:30:30,894
could keep going.

638
00:30:31,344 --> 00:30:33,344
There are a lot of zeros in this story.

639
00:30:33,444 --> 00:30:38,984
Thank you so much for taking the time to end war and disease, but if at

640
00:30:38,984 --> 00:30:43,204
any point you decide you're too busy, please press the share button on your

641
00:30:43,204 --> 00:30:46,904
glowing rectangle in case one of your friends have a free afternoon to end

642
00:30:46,904 --> 00:30:47,944
war and disease instead.

643
00:30:48,564 --> 00:30:52,904
And if you're too busy to even do that, please leave a really, really, really

644
00:30:52,904 --> 00:30:57,064
good rating and review so we overcome the pro -war algorithmic suppression

645
00:30:57,064 --> 00:31:00,624
and find someone with more spare time for ending wars and diseases.

646
00:31:01,184 --> 00:31:03,384
The good review doesn't have to be true, they don't check.

647
00:31:03,924 --> 00:31:07,984
But if you're too busy to even do that, the absolute least you could do

648
00:31:07,984 --> 00:31:13,604
is take 15 seconds to go to WarOnDisease.org and make your wishocratic allocation,

649
00:31:14,024 --> 00:31:17,584
telling us what fraction of humanity's resources should go to explosions

650
00:31:17,584 --> 00:31:19,044
versus clinical trials.

651
00:31:19,324 --> 00:31:19,824
And vote!

652
00:31:20,244 --> 00:31:24,504
If the 1% treaty passes, your vote will be personally to blame for saving

653
00:31:24,504 --> 00:31:29,124
2.6 lives and preventing 468,000 hours of suffering.

654
00:31:29,124 --> 00:31:31,824
Go to WarOnDisease.org right now.

655
00:31:32,224 --> 00:31:32,784
Love you, bye!
